    "descriptionChirho": "The Hebrew ordinal numeral (שְׁבִיעִי) meaning 'seventh,' used across 98 occurrences for the seventh day, month, year, or other sequential items. The two clusters differ only in the presence of a prefixed preposition (beth 'in/at the seventh') versus the bare or articled form ('the seventh'), which is a grammatical surface variation, not a semantic distinction. Evidence: eng 'the seventh / at the seventh,' spa 'el séptimo / a la séptima,' arb 'السَّابِعِ / في السّابِعَةِ,' kor '일곱째 / 일곱째에,' swa 'wa saba / mara ya saba,' hin 'सातवें / में सातवीं.' All translations render the same ordinal meaning throughout.",
